<th>HISTORY</th>
<td> H11177/03 -- OPR-K379-KR-03; Ian item (E8 in the DR) was detected approximately 985 meters east of the charted position of this item. Due to the shape of the target and the available information on the AWOIS Item, there is not conclusive evidence that they are the same item. It is recommended that the item be charted asa 53 foot obstruction at 28°19¿07.59 N, 96°17¿56.61 W.(NAD 83). However, during office review of the data, it was determined that Item E8 is a wreck and that it is AWOIS Item #10968. It was also determined that Item E8 does not have adequate multibeam development to determine an accurate least depth of the wreck. It is therefore recommended that the dangerous sunken wreck, PA in Latitude 28°19¿01.02 N, Longitude 96°18¿30.90 W (NAD 83) be deleted from the chart. It is further recommended that a dangerous sunken wreck, least depth unknown, AWOIS Item #10968 be charted at the present survey location in Latitude 28°19¿07.59 N, Longitude 96°17¿56.61 W (NAD 83) .Further investigation to determine a least depth for this item is advised. UPDATED 2/28/2006 JCM.

