 HISTORY
  H10938/99-- OPR-B330-RU;  AN UNCHARTED  WRECK WITH A LD OF 5 FEET WAS LOCATED IN LAT. 40-48-20.67N, LONG. 73-59-01.52W. IT IS DESCRIBED AS A SUNKEN BARGE ON THE END OF PIER 1 ON THE NEW JERSY SIDE OF THE RIVER. LD AND POSITION OBTAINED BY MB SONAR.  EVALUATOR RECOMMENDS CHARTING A 5WK AS SURVEYED. (ENT 9/26/02, SJV)

 S00003/03 -- S-B601-RU-02/03 HLS;  big wreck at end of pier in Survey Position: 040° 48' 19.876" N, 73° 59' 02.625" W (NAD 83). Too shoal to safely develop. Hydrographer Recommendation:Extend 5 Wk Southwest to reflect the true extents of the wreck as shown by side scan sonar. Office Notes: Concur. Extend limits of danger curve to include sw end of wreckage. Updated 9/5/2006 JCM</td>
</tr></table></center>]]></description>
