 HISTORY
  H11077/01-- SB904-WH; 200% SIDE SCAN SONAR AND 100% SWMB LOCATED AND IDENTIFIED SEVERAL WRECKS IN THE AREA GENERALLY REFERRED TO AS THE "WRECK SITE" .  DIVE OPS WERE CONDUCTED BY NOS AND NMFS IN ORDER TO IDENTIFY AND "SORT OUT" THE WRECKAGE AT THIS SITE. THIS ITEM IS DESCRIBED AS THE REMAINS OF A CRANE BARGE LYING BENEATH THE REMAINS OF THE F/V JANE & FLORA (SEE AWOIS # 11907). THE POSITION LISTED FOR THIS ITEM IS THE SAME AS THAT FOR THE JANE & FLORA. NO LD IS GIVEN FOR THIS ITEM. LAT. 41-31-24.76N, LONG. 70-40-38.95W. EVALUATOR RECOMMENDS REFERING TO THE JANE & FLORA FOR CHARTING DISPOSITION. ENT 7/14/03, SJV)</td>
