<td>  LNM29/73 (6/27/73)-- MASSACHUSETTS-GLOUCESTER INNER HARBOR-NORTH CHANNEL; THE USACE ADVISES THAT A 90-FOOT WOODEN BARGE IS SUNK IN APPROXIMATE LOCATION LAT. 42-36-52N, LONG. 70-39-18W.  SECURED TO A DILAPIDATED WHARF ADJACENT TO THE QUINCY MARKET COLD STORAGE AND WAREHOUSE CO., THE VESSEL IS ABOUT 20 FEET AWAY FROM THE WHARF AND EXTENDS TO THE CHANNEL.  IT IS MARKED WITH A LANTERN AT THE BOW AND STERN.  MARINERS SHOULD PROCEED WITH CAUTION WHEN TRANSITING THE AREA. (ENT 9/8/03, SJV)

H11277/03 -- 200% SSS and 100% MBES coverage was acquired over the navigable area of the search radius. A rectangular
object approximately 55 feet in length was found in the surveyed position. 
