<td></td>
</tr><tr bgcolor="">
<th>HISTORY</th>
<td> THE AWOIS POSITION IS THE APPROXIMATE CHARTED CENTER OF THE DUMP SITE. CHART LETTER 835/2000, 9/22/2000;  REPORTS THE EXISTANCE OF AN OCEAN DUMPING SITE EAST OF AND PARALLEL TO THE ATCHAFALAYA RIVER BAR CHANNEL APPROXIMATELY 18.5 MILES LONG WITH AN AVERAGE DEPTH OF 16 FT. THE CENTER OF THE DUMP SITE IS LOCATED IN LAT. 29/15/55.0 N, LON. 091/28/00 W. (NAD83). THE BOUNDARY COORDINATES OF THE RECTANGULAR SHAPED SITE ARE AS FOLLOWS: LAT. 29/20/59.92 N, LON. 91/23/33.23 W. (NAD83); LAT. 29/20/43.94 N, LON. 91/23/09.73 W. (NAD83); LAT. 29/08/15.46 N, LON. 91/34/51.02 W. (NAD83); LAT. 29/07/29.43 N, LON. 91/34/27.51 W. (NAD83).  INVESTIGATE SITE WITH IN 100 FT OF SHEET LIMITS. (ENTERED 12/03 BY KRW)</td>
</tr></table></center>]]></description>
<Point>
<coordinates>-91.466667,29.265278,0.0</coordinates>
</Point>
