  FE5/51--CS-362, ITEM 3; WK LOCATED AT POS.39-00-23N, 74-04-57W BY SONAR  ì
HUNG AT 80 FT, CLEARED TO 76 FT. NO DIVER INVESTIGATION. CHARTED AS WK. ì
CLEARED TO 12.5 FM.                                                          

 DESCRIPTION
                  
  24 NO. 337; TANKER, 9305 GT; SUNK BY SUBMARINE 1/25/42, LOCATED BY USCG ì
GENTIAN IN 126 FT OF WATER W/85 FT LD, AT POS. 39-00-30N, 74-05W         
 178 ANTHONY VRAIM, DIVER, OBSERVED LORAN-C 9960-X-26828.30, 9960-Y-42805.0, ì
(ASF CORRECTED 1981) POS.39-00-24N, 74-05-02W. LOCALLY KNOWN AS 28 MI WK.
  27 NO.238; TKR, 5505 NT, SUNK 1/25/42. LOCATED BY USCG GENTIAN IN 126 FT ì
STANDING 39 FT HIGH; LARGE OIL SLICK EVIDENT. PREVIOUSLY REPORTED AT ì
POS. LAT.39-02-00N, LONG.74-03-00W.                                      
  **** USCG SUNKEN TANKER PROJECT REPORT, 1967--USCG LOCATED AT 38-59-12N, ì
74-04-24W, DIVERS OBSERVED IN FAIR CONDITION BUT TANK SECTIONS OPEN, ì
IN 108 FT OF WATER. (POS NOT CONSIDERED RELIABLE DUE TO LARGE DIFFERENCES ì
FROM OTHER SOURCES. 1967 POS MAY BE BASED ON EARLY LORAN CHARTS WHICH ì
HAVE SUBSEQUENTLY BEEN IMPROVED.)                                        
  200 EDWARD E. SUAREZ, DIVER, OBSERVED LORAN-C 9960-X-26825.5, ì
9960-Y-42803.7,
  195  LORAN C RATES PROVIDED BY MR. RICHARD TARACKA, GREENWICH, ì
CT. POLICE DEPARTMENT, TEL NO 203-622-8020; 9960-X 26825.2, ì
9960-Y 42804.1. (ENTERED MSM 4/90)
  213  ALSO KNOWN AS THE 28 MILE WRECK; 9305 TON NORWEGIAN TANKER; ì
BUILT IN AMSTERDAM IN 1925 AND WAS OWNED BY WESTFAL, LARSEN AND ì
COMPANY; ON JANUARY 25, 1942, WHILE CARRYING A CARGO OF FUEL OIL ì
TO NEW YORK, SHIP WAS STRUCK AMIDSHIPS ON HER PORT SIDE BY ì
GERMAN TORPEDOES; RESTS IN 130 FT. OF WATER ALONG THE 29 FM. ì
CURVE; IN GOOD CONDITION, CONSIDERING THE NUMBER OF EXPLOSIONS ì
WHICH SANK HER; LORAN C RATES ARE THE SAME AS THOSE PROVIDED IN ì
200 ABOVE. (ENTERED MSM 7/90)</td>
