<td>
 HISTORY
  FE5/51--CS 326, ITEM 49; AN AREA EXTENDING ABOUT 1 1/4 MILES FROM ì
REPORTED POS CLEARED TO ED OF 98-102 FT. EXCEPT FOR 1040 FT BY 400 FT. ì
HOLIDAY BETWEEN STRIPS. HOLIDAY WAS RECONNED WITH FATHO. WK NOT FOUND ì
HYDROGRAPHER RECOMMENDS DELETION SINCE NOT FOUND. ALSO FACT THAT USCG AND ì
NAVY HAVE SEARCHED FOR WITH NEGATIVE RESULTS. ALSO RECOMMENDED THAT ì
NO FURTHER SEARCH BE CONDUCTED. CHARTED AS A 17 FM CLEARED SPOT.

 DESCRIPTION  
  24 NO.341; CARGO, 5152 GT,SUNK 3/8/42 BY SUBMARINE; POSITION ACCURACY 1-3 ì
MILES; REPORTED THRU 4TH ND, 10/1/42.                                    
  27 NO.537: CARGO 5152 NT: SUNK 3/8/42, PREVIOUSLY REPORTED AT ì
LAT.39-10N, LONG.72-02-00W.
  178 PRIVATE DIVER HAS SEARCHED FOR 6 YEARS (1981) WITH NEGATIVE RESULTS.     
SAYS 1 MAN IN THE AREA KNEW OF LOCATION BUT DIED WITHOUT DISCLOSING.     
  195 LORAN C RATES PROVIDED BY MR. RICHARD TARACKA, GREENWICH, ì
CT. POLICE DEPARTMENT, TEL NO 203-622-8020; 9960-X 26721.0, ì
9960-Y 42852.0. (ENTERED MSM 4/90)</td>
</tr></table></center>]]></description>
