<td></td>
</tr><tr bgcolor="#E3E3F3">
<th>YEARSUNK</th>
<td></td>
</tr><tr bgcolor="">
<th>HISTORY</th>
<td>LNM 19/92--4/28/92;  THE S/V LUMINA, PREVIOUSLY REPORTED SUNK IN THE SAVANNAH RIVER ENTRANCE, WAS MOVED APPROXIMATELY 150 YARDS AND 140 DEGREES TRUE FROM THE SAVANNAH RIVER SOUTH JETTY LIGHT TO APPROXIMATE POSITION 32-02-00N 80-51-00W IN 9 FEET OF WATER.  THE WRECK WAS MARKED WITH AN ALL AROUND WHITE LIGHT ATTACHED TO THE MAST.  IT WAS REPORTED THAT AT HIGH WATER, ONLY 4 FEET OF THE MAST WAS VISIBLE.  THERE WAS A TEMPORARY LIGHTED BUOY WR1 MARKING THE TOP HALF OF THE MAST AND BOOM.</td>
</tr></table></center>]]></description>
<Point>
<coordinates>-80.85,32.033333,0.0</coordinates>
</Point>
</Placemark>
