<td> H11045/04 -- OPR-B340-RU; AN INVESTIGATION FOR THIS ITEM WAS REQUESTED BY THE SUFFOLK POLICE DEPARTMENT. IT WAS IDENTIFIED DURING MAINSCHEME SIDE SCAN OPERATIONS IN POSITION: LATITUDE 41°02¿00.529 N, LONGITUDE 073°13¿28.975 W [NAD83]. SWMB REVEALED A LEAST DEPTH OF 21.84 METERS CORRECTED WITH VERIFIED TIDES IN 27.95 METERS OF WATER. IMAGERY INDICATED THE PRESENCE OF AN AIRPLANE WRECK. DIVE INVESTIGATION REVEALED THE ITEM TO BE A TWIN-ENGINE CESSNA. DIVER'S LEAST DEPTH NOT TAKEN. THE EVALUATOR RECOMMENDS CHARTING THIS ITEM AS A DANGEROUS 71 OBSTRUCTION. UPDATED 12/20/04 JCM.</td>
