<td></td>
</tr><tr bgcolor="">
<th>HISTORY</th>
<td>  L1644/80-- JULY 1980; LOCAL KNOWLEDGE AND A SHIPWRECK CHART OF LAKE MICHIGAN INFORMED FIELD PARTY OF THE WRECKS EXISTENCE.  GEO. MORLEY, A 192 FT CARGO VESSEL WHICH BURNED AND EXPLODED IN 1897. UPON INVESTIGATION OF THE AREA, A BUOY WAS FOUND MARKING THE STERN END OF THE WRECK, WHICH WAS ALSO WAS THE POINT OF LEAST DEPTH OF 4 FT.  THE WRECK EXTENDS NORTHWARD FROM POSITION 405 APPROX 60 M, CONFIRMED BY RECON INVESTIGATION OF THE AREA USING THE FATHOMETER. (ENTERED 3/05 CEH)
  F00502/06-- OPR-Y387-NRT4-05; Item was not investigated because the area was to shallow for SSS.  Retain as charted. (Updated CEH 11/2008)</td>
</tr></table></center>]]></description>
