</tr><tr bgcolor="">
<th>HISTORY</th>
<td>History

  LNM50/83 -- On 12 December 1983, the 74 foot fishing vessel, MISS DIANA, burned and sank offshore of Kill Devil Hills, North Carolina.  The vessel appeared to have sunk bow first with stern of vessel approximately 4 feet below the surface.  The vessel was last reported in approximate position 36/01.3 N lat, 75/38.2 W lon (NAD27).  A subsequent search failed to locate the vessel.  Mariners were advised to transit the area with extreme caution.  (CG 07APR05)</td>
