</tr><tr bgcolor="">
<th>SOUNDING_TYPE</th>
<td>Meters and tenths</td>
</tr><tr bgcolor="#E3E3F3">
<th>YEARSUNK</th>
<td></td>
</tr><tr bgcolor="">
<th>HISTORY</th>
<td>F00225/1975; NOS--NOAA Ships RUDE & HECK conducted wire drag and diver ops and located a clam boat approx 90 ft in length with a beam of 25 ft lying on its STBD side in 64 ft of water.  Numerous WWII surplus submarine net buoys were lying next to the Wk.  Effective depth of Subm Wk found to be 54 feet.

H09972/1981; NOS--NOAA Ship Peirce conducted VBES surveys in the area using reduced line spacing.  The Subm Wk was not located and was retained as charted.

H12203/2010; NOS -- NOAA Ship THOMAS JEFFERSON found charted "Obstn" using 200% Klein 5000 SSS.  Least Depth found using MBES.  Charted "Obstn" corresponds to identified wreck. (LAH 08/07/2012)  

</td>
</tr></table></center>]]></description>
<Point>
<coordinates>-75.5691667,36.728528,0.0</coordinates>
</Point>
