<th>HISTORY</th>
<td>
 HISTORY
  H5078/30WD--PROJ. NO.64; WRECKAGE, 32FT, (CHARTED AS WRECK CLEARED 31FT) IN ì
LAT 40-55-52.50N, LONG 73-36-13.90W. WK IS IN 47FT OF WATER ON A SOFT MUD ì
BOTTOM.
  FE318SS/88--OPR-B660-HE-88; 200% SIDE SCAN SONAR COVERAGE FOR ì
75 M RADIUS AT 100 M RANGE; ONE SIGNIFICANT TARGET IDENTIFIED IN ì
LAT 40-55-53.418N, LONG 73-36-13.840W; DIVERS FOUND THE BROKEN ì
AND DETERIORATED REMAINS OF A 100 X 25 FT. STEEL HULLED VESSEL; ì
ONLY PROMINENT FEATURE REMAINING IS THE LOWER PORTION OF THE HULL ì
AND THE ATTACHED RIBBING; SUNKEN INTO THE BOTTOM; ORIGIN AND ì
PURPOSE WERE NOT DETERMINED; LOCALLY KNOWN AS "BABY DOLL"; RISES ì
3 FT. ABOVE THE BOTTOM; LORAN C RATES: 9960-W 15345.0, 9960-X ì
26880.2, 9960-Y 43954.9, 9960-Z 60004.1; HYDROGRAPHER AND ì
EVALUATOR RECOMMENDED CHARTING A NONDANGEROUS WRECK WITH LEAST ì
DEPTH OF 46 FT. IN SURVEY POSITION. (UPDATED MSM 12/89)
  H10612/95-- OPR-B389-CN; WRECK LOCATED BY MULTIBEAM ECHO ì
SOUNDER IN LAT. 40-55-52.42N, LONG. 73-36-13.49W. DEPTH OF 13.8 ì
METERS (45 FEET). LIES 31 METERS (102 FEET), 164 DEG. FROM AWOIS ì
POSITION. EVALUATOR RECOMMENDS REVISING 46 WK TO A 45 WK AS ì
SURVEYED. WRECK DOES NOT APPEAR TO BE IN TWO PIECES AS ì
INTERPRETED FROM MULTIBEAM AND SIDE SCAN RECORDS. (UP 7/25/97, ì
SJV)
   S00002/02--S-B600-RU--Sunken wooden ship; Delete 45ft Wk in Lat. 40°55'52.42", Long. 73°36'13.49", Chart 45ft Wk in Lat. 40°55'52.57", Long. 73°36'13.75" (RES 8/13/07).</td>
</tr></table></center>]]></description>
