<th>YEARSUNK</th>
<td></td>
</tr><tr bgcolor="">
<th>HISTORY</th>
<td> SURVEY REQUIREMENT COMMENTS
  DIVER INVESTIGATE TO VERIFY IDENTITY AND DETERMINE LEAST DEPTH.

 HISTORY
  NM29/49--THE FISHING VESSEL DORIS IS REPORTED TO HAVE SUNK IN ì
LAT 41-22-15N, LONG 71-23-19W.
  NM51/65--WRECK NON-EXISTENT, DANGEROUS WRECK CHARTED IN PA LAT ì
41-22-15N, LONG 71-23-18W DOES NOT EXIST; EXPUNGED FROM CHART.
  FE194WD/64--OPR-444-ITEM PR-15; AREA OF WK CLEARED TO 97 FT ED. ì
(SEXTANT-DUAL VESSEL CONTROL AT 1:80,000); WRECK CHARTED IN LAT.41-22-15N, ì
LONG.71-23-18.6W NOT FOUND BUT A WRECK IN LAT 41-23-12.6N, LONG ì
71-22-18.6W (5000 YARDS, 165 DEGREES TRUE FROM BRENTON REEF ì
LIGHT) HUNG AT 88 FT. AND CLEARED WITH 85 FT.; FATHOMETER ì
INDICATED A WRECK; BELIEVED TO BE ITEM PR-15; TRACES OF RED LEAD ì
AND SCRAPE MARKS WERE FOUND ON GROUND WIRE; EVALUATOR RECOMMENDED ì
DELETING CHARTED WRECK AND ADDING WRECK FOUND BY THIS SURVEY. ì
(UPDATED MSM 6/89)
  FE367SS/91--OPR-B660-RU; WRECK LOCATED BY SIDE SCAN SONAR WITH ì
A LEAST DEPTH OF 29.8M (98FT) IN POS. LAT.41-23-11.75N, ì
LONG.71-22-30.07W (NAD 83). ITEM WAS LOCATED JUST OUTSIDE THE ì
ASSIGNED SEARCH RADIUS, VERY CLOSE TO THE LORAN RATES GIVEN BY ì
MR. TARACKA. EVALUATOR CONCLUDES THAT THE SONARGRAMS SHOW THE ì
WRECK TO BE APPROX. 54M (177 FT) IN LENGTH AND THAT IT APPEARS TO ì
BE THE SUBMARINE L-8. HYDROGRAPHER/EVALUATOR RECOMMEND THAT THIS ì
WRECK SHOULD SUPERSEDE THE CURRENTLY CHARTED 85FT WRECK. ì
(UPDATED 8/93 MCR)

 DESCRIPTION
  24   NO.297; TRAWLER; SUNK 1949; POSITION ACCURACY WITHIN 1 MILE              
  193  LORAN C RATES PROVIDED BY MR. RICHARD TARACKA, GREENWICH, ì
CT. POLICE DEPARTMENT, TEL NO. 203-622-8007; 9960-X 25776.0, ì
9960-Y 43959.0; IDENTIFIED AS SUBMARINE L-8. (ENTERED MSM 8/89)</td>
</tr></table></center>]]></description>
