<td>Meters and tenths</td>
</tr><tr bgcolor="#E3E3F3">
<th>YEARSUNK</th>
<td></td>
</tr><tr bgcolor="">
<th>HISTORY</th>
<td> HISTORY
  NM31/45--BUOY ESTABLISHED 4745 YARDS 210 DEGREES FROM TWO MILE ì
ROCK BEACON TO MARK A WRECK; BUOY LIES 100 YARDS 167 DEGREES FROM ì
THE WRECK WHICH HAS A MAST PROJECTING 20 FT. ABOVE THE WATER; PA ì
LAT 41-27-30N, LONG 71-06-10W. (ENTERED MSM 4/89)
  NM30/48--WK CHARTED AT LAT.41-27-33N, LONG.71-06-11W, IS LOCATED 4,600 YDS  ì
216 DEGS, 25 MIN FROM TWO-MILE ROCK DAYBEACON. THERE IS A MINIMUM DEPTH OVER ì
IT OF 14 FT AT MLW, THE MASTS ARE NO LONGER IN PLACE; LAT ì
41-27-42N, LONG 71-06-23W.
  FE194WD/64--OPR-444; ITEM PR-25; DISCREDITED 14 FT WK AT LAT.41-27-42N,  ì
LONG.71-06-22.8W, CHARTED POS. CLEARED 26 FT ED. DRAG HUNG ON SALVAGE BUOYS ì
SOUTH OF CHARTED POS. SALVAGER REPORTED ONLY BOW INTACT. ì
RECOMMENDED 43 FT WK BE CHARTED AT LAT.41-27-35.4N, LONG.71-06-15.6W, ì
FATHOMETER DEPTH. SEXTANT-DUAL VESSEL CONTROL AT 1:20,000.
  NM1/66--RECOMMENDED WK COVERED 14 FT AT LAT.41-27-42N, LONG.71-06-21W BE  ì
DELETED FROM THE CHART.
  CL1019/66--C&GS WAINWRIGHT & HILGARD; SAME DATA AS FE194WD/64 (UNREVIEWED), ì
NAMES VESSEL AS ST. CLAIR, A DESTROYER.
  FE207WD/67--OPR-444; ITEM PR-25; LOCATED WK AT LAT.41-27-37N, ì
LONG.71-06-17W, SEXTANT-DUAL VESSEL CONTROL AT 1;20,000. DIVER INVESTIGATED, ì
FOUND AN 8X18 FT SECTION OF BOW APPROX. 15 FT OFF THE BOTTOM. LEAST SOUNDED ì
DEPTH 47 FT, CLEARED 44 FT.
  FE375SS/92--OPR-B660-RU; WRECK LOCATED BY SIDE SCAN SONAR AND ì
FOUND TO BE SEVERELY DETERIORATED, SCATTERED, AND FLATTENED. ì
EXTENT OF WRECKAGE WAS DEVELOPED BY ECHO SOUNDER USING 10M LINE ì
SPACING. LEAST DEPTH WAS DETERMINED TO BE 15.6M (51.2 FT) IN POS. ì
LAT.41-27-37.49N, LONG.71-06-14.87 (NAD 83). DIVER INVESTIGATION ì
WAS INEFFECTIVE DUE TO POOR VISIBILITY AND STRONG CURRENTS. ì
EVALUATOR RECOMMENDS TO CHART DANGEROUS SUBMERGED WRECKAGE WITH A ì
DEPTH OF 51 FT (15.6M) IN ABOVE GP. (UPDATED 1/93 MCR)
 DESCRIPTION
  24   NO.561; SUNK 1945; POSITION ACCURACY WITHIN 1 MILE; WD CLEARED ì
TO 14 FT.</td>
</tr></table></center>]]></description>
