<td>03245
DESCRIPTION
**** WASHINGTON POST, DEC. 14, 1983; SPANISH GALLEON FOUNDERED OFF MD-VA COAST
     IN 1750; 50 GUN FRIGATE, CARGO OF MAHOGANY PLANKS AND TOBACCO (SPANISH   
     ARCHIVES). WRECK ASSUMED TO BE BURIED BY MIGRATING DUNES AND SHIFTING    
     COASTLINE. OCEAN RECOVERY OPERATIONS INC. BACKING RESEARCH EFFORTS.      
     JOHN L. AMRHEIN JR. AND WILSON BANE ARE POINTS OF CONTACT. MAGNETOMETER  
     READINGS HAVE BEEN POSITIVE AT THE SITE. SITE IS WITHIN CHINCOTEAGUE     
     NATIONAL WILDLIFE REFUGE, U.S. FISH AND WILDLIFE SERVICE. (SEE NOS CHART 
     12211 AND GS QUAD BOXIRON, MD-VA, 7.5 MIN).                              

SURVEY REQUIREMENTS
NOT DETERMINED                                                                
</td>
