<td>  LNM49/01--13TH CGD, 12/04/01;  ADD DANGEROUS WRECK,  WITH MAST IN POS. 46 15 12N, 123 58 09W. ENTERED 4/02 MCR
  FE486/02--OPR-N438-NRB; A FULL INVESTIGATION WAS DONE FOR THE 300 RADIUS WITH 200 PERCENT SIDE SCAN SONAR AT LAT. 46/15/12N, LONG 123/58/09W.  NO EVIDENCE OF THE WRECK WAS FOUND. THE SEARCH WAS EXPANDED, BASED ON REPORTS THAT THE WRECK WAS SPOTTED APPROXIMATELY 75 YARDS EAST OF CHINOOK CHANNEL LIGHT 1.  THE SUBMERGED WRECK, 30 FT LONG AND LYING ON ITS SIDE WITH THE BOW POINTED NORTH,  WAS LOCATED AT LAT. 46/15/29.746N, LONG. 123/58/14.740W.  THE LEAST DEPTH WAS CALCULATED WITH THE DIVERS LEAST DEPTH GAUGE AT 11.5 FT.  LOCAL SOURCE IDENTIFIED THE VESSEL AS "LOG DOG".  (UPDATED 3/05 CEH)</td>
</tr></table></center>]]></description>
