<td></td>
</tr><tr bgcolor="#E3E3F3">
<th>YEARSUNK</th>
<td></td>
</tr><tr bgcolor="">
<th>HISTORY</th>
<td>  ****  EMAIL FROM LCDR DOUG BAIRD ON 3/26/02: The F/V Steamer was scuttled Friday, March 22, 2002 at approximate position 55-17.1' N, 131-36.5' W.  The vessel is 70 ft LOA, built in 1901 with a wood hull.  The vessel was stripped of most machinery and deck equipment before it was sunk by Peter Vournas.  This info was relayed to me by personnel from USCG 17th District.  The position has the wreck on the southwest edge of survey H-10988.

(ENTERED 3/26/02 BY MBH - UPDATE BY LMN ISSUED BY 17CGD WILL BE NECESSARY WHEN PUBLISHED)</td>
</tr></table></center>]]></description>
<Point>
<coordinates>-131.608333,55.285,0.0</coordinates>
</Point>
