<th>RECRD</th>
<td>53957</td>
</tr><tr bgcolor="">
<th>VESSLTERMS</th>
<td>WRECK</td>
</tr><tr bgcolor="#E3E3F3">
<th>FEATURE_TYPE</th>
<td>Wreck - Submerged, dangerous to surface navigation</td>
</tr><tr bgcolor="">
<th>LATDEC</th>
<td>47.373424</td>
</tr><tr bgcolor="#E3E3F3">
<th>LONDEC</th>
<td>-122.456427</td>
</tr><tr bgcolor="">
<th>GP_QUALITY</th>
<td>High</td>
</tr><tr bgcolor="#E3E3F3">
<th>DEPTH</th>
<td>2.53</td>
</tr><tr bgcolor="">
<th>SOUNDING_TYPE</th>
<td>Meters and tenths</td>
</tr><tr bgcolor="#E3E3F3">
<th>YEARSUNK</th>
<td></td>
</tr><tr bgcolor="">
<th>HISTORY</th>
<td>H11551(2007)--MBES least depth on wreck of ~35' power yacht. Dive report: ~35 foot power yacht sunk on its mooring. The vessel's superstructure was of wood construction. The age of the electronic equipment aboard and relatively light
marine growth suggests that the vessel sank relatively recently (within the last 5 years). No identifying markings were found. Least depth ~2.53m (1fm 2ft). Entered by RES on 5/4/10.</td>
</tr></table></center>]]></description>
<Point>
<coordinates>-122.456427,47.373424,0.0</coordinates>
</Point>
</Placemark>
