<td>
 HISTORY
  H5219/32WD--12 FT SOUNDING TAKEN ON HANG IDENTIFIED AS WRECKAGE ì
IN LAT 41-02-24.3N, LONG 73-28-01.3W; POSITION SCALED FROM SURVEY ì
AT 1:20,000 SCALE. (ENTERED MSM 5/88)
  FE320SS/88--OPR-B660-RU-88; COULD NOT BE FULLY INVESTIGATED BY ì
RUDE DUE TO THE SHALLOW DEPTHS AND THE POTENTIAL FOR HAZARDOUS ì
OBSTRUCTIONS; DURING OFFICE PROCESSING OF THE INVESTIGATION THAT ì
WAS ACCOMPLISHED, TWO CONTACTS WERE FOUND (ALSO SEE ITEM 7764); ì
ONE CONTACT IN LAT 41-02-24.02N, LONG 73-27-58.99W WITH AN ì
ESTIMATED LEAST DEPTH OF 21FT. IS LOCATED 90.5M EAST OF THIS ITEM ì
AND MAY BE THE REMAINS OF THIS WRECKAGE; EVALUATOR RECOMMENDED ì
NOT CHARTING THIS ITEM PENDING FURTHER INVESTIGATION BY THE FIELD ì
PARTY. (UPDATED MSM 5/90)
  H10565/94-- OPR-B285-94 ; 50-METER RADIUS ES SEARCH  NEGATIVE.  DISCUSSIONS WITH A REPRESENTATIVE OF "TALLMUDGE FISHERIES" WHICH OPERATES CLAM AND OYSTER DREDGES IN THE AREA INDICATED NO KNOWLEDGE OF ANY SNAGS OR OBSTRUCTIONS IN THE AREA.  THE HYDROGRAPHER RECOMMENDS DELETING THE CHARTED 12 "WRECKAGE".  THE EVALUATOR DID NOT CONCUR AND CONSIDERED THE INVESTIGATION WAS NOT ADEQUATE FOR DISPROVAL. THE FEATURE WAS BROUGHT FORWARD TO THE PRESENT SURVEY AND ADDITIONAL WORK IS RECOMMENDED. (UP 11/29/04, SJV)</td>
</tr></table></center>]]></description>
