<th>HISTORY</th>
<td>
 HISTORY
  NM17/42--ON 4/18/42, A VESSEL REPORTED STILING A SUBMERGED OBSTRUCTION AT
  NM DATED 6/27/56 
  FE157/57WD--FE16/57WD; CLEARED TO 9.5 FMS, NO HANG. 
  H9155/70--OPR-438; NOT FOUND ON MAINSCHEME.                                   

 DESCRIPTION
                
  24 NO.406; SUBMARINE, 500 GT, SUNK 4/15/42; POS. ACCURACY 1 MILE AT ì
     35-53-12N, 75-17W, LOCATED 8/24/44.
  27 NO.294; LOCATED BY ESF AT POS.35-53-12N, 75-17W; PREVIOUSLY REPORTED TO ì
     BE AT POS.35-55N, 75-15W.                                                
 177 NO.406; SUNK 4/14/42                                                     
 180 COMPLETE HISTORY TO INCLUDE ACCOUNT OF SINKING AND PARTIAL SALVAGE       
 195 LORAN-C RATES: 9960 CHAIN; 26917.0X AND 40713.6Y (RATES DIFFER FROM POS. ì
     LISTED ABOVE) WRECK LIES IN 95-FT DEPTHS ON ITS STARBOARD SIDE AT A 80 ì
     DEG. ANGLE. THE CONNING TOWER IS THE HIGHEST PT OFF THE BOTTOM.
**** ROBERT HOLLOWEL, COMMERCIAL FISHERMAN, 804-587-0103: VERIFIED LOCATION ì
     6/30/82. DIVER INSPECTION SHOWS ONLY CONNING TOWER VISIBLE ABOVE BOTTOM, ì
     LARGE SCOUR DEVELOPING ALONGSIDE, THINKS SUB WILL EVENTUALLY FALL INTO ì
     AND BE COVERED.                                                          
**** STEVEN PFAFF (919-759-9525); ALSO HAS IDENTICAL VERIFIED LORAN NUMBERS.</td>
