<th>HISTORY</th>
<td>
 HISTORY
  NM32/65--COE ADVISES THAT THE WRECK OF THE FISHING VESSEL ì
WAMSETTA IS LOCATED IN PA LAT 41-18N, LONG 70-52W IN 65 FT. OF ì
WATER.
  NM41/66--WRECK WITH 15 FT. OVER THE MAST HAS BEEN REPORTED IN ì
LAT 41-19-06N, LONG 70-50-18W.
  NM43/66--INVESTIGATION BY C&GS SHOWS THE WRECK PREVIOUSLY ì
REPORTED IN LAT 41-18N, LONG 70-52W AND LAT 41-19-06N, LONG ì
70-50-18W HAS BEEN LOCATED IN LAT 41-09-06N, LONG 70-50-12W; ì
CLEARED TO 45 FT. (ENTERED MSM 3/89)
  FE207WD/66 (FE3/67WD)--WRECK WAS FOUND IN LAT 41-19-03N, LONG ì
70-50-11W; TOPS OF TWO MASTS WERE FOUND TO BE AT 10 AND 12 FT ì
MLW; CABLES CONNECTING MASTS TO WRECK WERE DISCONNECTED AND MASTS ì
WERE TOWED CLOSE TO THE BEACH SOUTH OF GAY HEAD; REMAINING ì
WRECKAGE IS BROKEN UP AND WITHIN 5 FT. OF THE BOTTOM; WRECKAGE ì
CLEARED BY 45 FT.; REVIEWER RECOMMENDED CHARTING 45 FT. CLEARED ì
DEPTH AT POSITION FOUND BY THIS SURVEY. (ENTERED MSM 4/89)
</td>
</tr></table></center>]]></description>
