<th>HISTORY</th>
<td>  LNM1/72--A 36-FT. BARGE WITH PILE DRIVER ATTACHED HAS SUNK IN APPROX. 18
FT., IN THE VICINITY OF THE ENTRANCE TO LITTLE CREEK HARBOR; POS. DOUBTFUL.
  1969 R/H INVESTIGATION 20-2-69 (UNPROCESSED);  BOTTOM LITTERED WITH
MISC. DEBRIS
  H9910/80--OPR-D103-MI-80; 1:10,000 SCALE SURVEY; DEL NORTE CONRTOL (R/R, R/A)
ECHO SOURNDER W/50M LINE SPACING, DID NOT LOCATE WK; H9255WD DID NOT LOCATE
BUT CLEARED WK TO 16FT IN 19-21FT DEPTHS; RECOMMEND RETAIN SUBM DANG WK W/ED
AND NOTE (CLEARED TO 16FT); NOT CONSIDERED DISPROVED BY THIS SURVEY. (ENTERED
10/15/84, MSM)</td>
